# Copy to .env.local (git-ignored) and fill in what you need. Nothing here is required to play on testnet with no
# AI agent: the game works with every one of these unset.

# --- Which chain the web app talks to (lib/chain/config.ts) ---
# "sandbox" for a local near-sandbox started by contracts/sandbox (npm run dev:chain); unset or anything else = testnet.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_NEAR_NETWORK=testnet
# NEXT_PUBLIC_NEAR_RPC=https://test.rpc.fastnear.com
# NEXT_PUBLIC_DEEDLORDS_CONTRACT=game.deedlords.testnet
# NEXT_PUBLIC_ARENA_CONTRACT=arena.deedlords.testnet
# A local helper that can sign for test accounts and hand out test NEAR (contracts/sandbox: play:testnet or dev:chain's
# own stub). Point the web app at it with NEXT_PUBLIC_DEEDLORDS_DEV_URL; leave unset in a public deployment.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_DEEDLORDS_DEV_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8792

# --- Which model an AI agent asks for a turn or a playbook (games/co-ty-phu/agent/llm.ts) ---
# Checked in order: an explicit endpoint, then NEARAI_API_KEY (NEAR AI Cloud), then OPENAI_API_KEY. None set: an agent
# plays by its playbook's arithmetic alone, and "Write playbook" is unavailable.
# DEEDLORDS_LLM_BASE_URL=https://api.shopaikey.com/v1
# DEEDLORDS_LLM_API_KEY=
# DEEDLORDS_LLM_MODEL=gpt-4.1-mini
# Extra models an owner may choose in the Co-pilot stub, comma-separated, as the service names them; the one above is
# always included and does not need repeating here.
# DEEDLORDS_LLM_MODELS=gpt-4.1-mini,gpt-4.1-nano,gemini-2.5-flash,gemini-2.5-flash-lite
# What a seat driven by this model is labelled with on the table; defaults to the model's own name.
# DEEDLORDS_LLM_LABEL=
# NEARAI_API_KEY=
# OPENAI_API_KEY=

# --- A ceiling on how often this server pays for a model call (games/co-ty-phu/agent/rateLimit.ts) ---
# Protects the owner's bill on a public deployment: past the limit, a turn plays by its playbook instead of asking the
# model (never refused), and "Write playbook" answers 429 instead of calling the model. 0 disables a limit.
# Turn advice (app/api/agent): per caller / 10 min, and across every caller / hour.
# DEEDLORDS_LLM_IP_LIMIT=20
# DEEDLORDS_LLM_GLOBAL_LIMIT=300
# Writing a playbook (app/api/agent/playbook) costs more tokens per call, so its ceiling is tighter.
# DEEDLORDS_PLAYBOOK_IP_LIMIT=5
# DEEDLORDS_PLAYBOOK_GLOBAL_LIMIT=60

# --- Free play: who pays for free tables (lib/chain/sponsor.ts, app/api/relay, app/api/free) ---
# The account that opens free tables (its storage deposit, returned at settlement), relays their players' signed moves
# as meta-transactions (its gas) and plays the house agent's seat. Unset: no free tables, everything else works.
# `node contracts/sandbox/sponsor.js run` creates one on testnet. Give it little: what it holds is what a leaked key,
# or a hole in the relayer's rules, can cost.
# DEEDLORDS_SPONSOR_ACCOUNT=free.deedlords.testnet
# Its secret key (ed25519:…). Leave unset on your own machine: the key is then read from
# ~/.near-credentials/<network>/<account>.json, where NEAR's own tools keep it. Never commit it.
# DEEDLORDS_SPONSOR_KEY=
# The model the house agent asks for its turn, one of DEEDLORDS_LLM_MODELS; unset, it plays by the default playbook.
# DEEDLORDS_HOUSE_MODEL=gemini-2.5-flash-lite
# Ceilings on what the sponsor pays for (0 disables one). Relayed calls and house-agent turns: per caller and per
# game account / 10 min, and across everyone / hour. A relayed move burns about 0.0005 NEAR.
# DEEDLORDS_RELAY_IP_LIMIT=400
# DEEDLORDS_RELAY_GLOBAL_LIMIT=6000
# Free tables opened and new game accounts brought on chain: per caller / 10 min, and across everyone / hour.
# DEEDLORDS_FREE_IP_LIMIT=6
# DEEDLORDS_FREE_GLOBAL_LIMIT=120
# How many free tables may be open at once; each holds 0.06 NEAR of the sponsor's until it is settled.
# DEEDLORDS_FREE_TABLES=12

# --- Sign-in with Google through NEAR Auth (lib/chain/nearAuth.ts; needs a sponsor, above) ---
# The Auth0 application that signs people in: a public value, not a secret. On testnet NEAR Auth publishes a shared
# one for development (docs.auth.near.org/resources/testnet); it only accepts pages served at http://localhost:3000.
# Unset: no Google button. A public deployment needs its own (docs.auth.near.org/home/apply).
# NEXT_PUBLIC_NEAR_AUTH_CLIENT_ID=np8paqIpMWmNbzT4xAvOOapZBjsOpptl
# NEXT_PUBLIC_NEAR_AUTH_DOMAIN=login.testnet.fast-auth.com
# Key grants signed through NEAR Auth, each a 300 Tgas call of the sponsor's: per caller / 10 min, everyone / hour.
# DEEDLORDS_GRANT_IP_LIMIT=4
# DEEDLORDS_GRANT_GLOBAL_LIMIT=60
# Stakes and withdrawals signed through NEAR Auth, the same call: per caller and per account / 10 min, everyone / hour.
# DEEDLORDS_SIGN_IP_LIMIT=20
# DEEDLORDS_SIGN_GLOBAL_LIMIT=300
